          "claim": "Along any piecewise smooth path with height coordinate $t$, its hyperbolic length is at least $\\int |dt|/t$, since the metric contains the term $dt^2/t^2$. A path escaping the end has $t\\to\\infty$, so this lower bound diverges as $\\log t$. Thus the end is at infinite distance and is complete toward its ideal end.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F1",
