        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "For a loop $\\gamma$ on the link, the linear part of its similarity holonomy is $H(\\gamma)$: transporting a tangent vector across each corner multiplies it by the corner parameter or its reciprocal according to the side used. The basis loops have multiplier $1$, so the linear holonomy is trivial on $\\pi_1(T)$, since every loop is a word in that basis.",
