          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every real $\\theta$, $\\Lambda$ is continuous, odd, and $\\pi$-periodic, with $\\Lambda(\\pi/2)=0$ and $$ \\Lambda(2\\theta)=2\\Lambda(\\theta)+2\\Lambda(\\theta+\\pi/2). $$ For $0\\le\\theta\\le\\pi$, $$ \\Lambda(\\theta)=\\frac12\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{\\sin(2n\\theta)}{n^2}. $$ In particular, $$ \\Lambda(\\pi/3)=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty} \\left(\\frac1{(3k+1)^2}-\\frac1{(3k+2)^2}\\right). $$ For every integer $N\\ge1$, the positive remainder after the terms $k=0,\\ldots,N$ is at most $\\sqrt3/(72N^2)$.",
