          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Integrating the volume density in $t$ gives $\\operatorname{Vol}(\\mathcal O_\\zeta)=\\int_0^{\\cos\\zeta}\\int_0^{x\\tan\\zeta}\\frac{dy\\,dx}{2(1-x^2-y^2)}$. For fixed $x$, put $A=\\sqrt{1-x^2}$; since $x\\tan\\zeta<A$ for $0\\le x<\\cos\\zeta$, the inner integral is $\\frac1{4A}\\log\\frac{A+x\\tan\\zeta}{A-x\\tan\\zeta}$.",
