        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-knot-exterior-homology-and-longitude",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $K:S^1\\to S^3$ be a smooth oriented embedding and write its quotient normal bundle as $\\nu_K=K^*TS^3/dK(TS^1)$. Choose an orientation-preserving trivialization $\\nu_K\\cong S^1\\times\\mathbb R^2$ and a tubular map $\\Phi:\\Omega\\to S^3$, meaning a smooth embedding from an open neighbourhood $\\Omega\\subseteq\\nu_K$ of the zero section onto an open neighbourhood of $K(S^1)$ with $\\Phi(s,0)=K(s)$, such that in these product coordinates $\\Omega$ contains $S^1\\times D^2_{2\\epsilon}$ for some $\\epsilon>0$. Here $D^2_r=\\{z\\in\\mathbb R^2:\\|z\\|\\le r\\}$. Set $N(K)=\\Phi(S^1\\times D^2_\\epsilon)$, $E_K=S^3\\setminus\\operatorname{int}N(K)$, $T_K=\\partial E_K$, and let $i:T_K\\hookrightarrow E_K$ be inclusion, $p:T_K\\to S^1$ the product projection, and $\\mu$ the positive boundary of a normal disk, using the normal-plane orientation determined by the orientations of $K$ and $S^3$. A class is primitive if it is not $m$ times another class for any integer $|m|>1$. Then $H_1(E_K;\\mathbb Z)\\cong\\mathbb Z$ is generated by $[\\mu]$. The kernel of $i_*:H_1(T_K;\\mathbb Z)\\to H_1(E_K;\\mathbb Z)$ is a primitive rank-one direct summand generated by a unique class $[\\lambda]$ with $p_*[\\lambda]=1\\in H_1(S^1;\\mathbb Z)$. It has a simple closed representative, is the preferred longitude, and $([\\mu],[\\lambda])$ is a basis of $H_1(T_K;\\mathbb Z)$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
