        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-smooth-schoenflies-for-embedded-two-sphere-in-s-three",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume countable choice. Let $S\\subset S^3$ be the image of a smooth embedding of the standard $S^2$. There is a smooth ambient isotopy $H_t:S^3\\to S^3$, with $H_0=\\operatorname{id}$, such that $H_1(S)$ is the standard equatorial sphere $E$. In particular $S^3\\setminus S$ has exactly two components. Their closures $B_+$ and $B_-$ are smoothly embedded standard closed $3$-balls with common boundary $S$. If $D_+$ and $D_-$ denote the standard closed hemispheres bounded by $E$, the labels can be chosen so that the restrictions $H_1:B_\\pm\\to D_\\pm$ are diffeomorphisms with the same boundary restriction $H_1|_S:S\\to E$. Thus the ball identifications are compatible on their boundary and on a common two-sided collar of that boundary.",
