        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-regular-ideal-tetrahedron-volume",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Every regular ideal tetrahedron in hyperbolic three-space has volume $$ v_3=3\\Lambda(\\pi/3) =\\frac{3\\sqrt3}{4}\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty} \\left(\\frac1{(3k+1)^2}-\\frac1{(3k+2)^2}\\right). $$",
          "uses": [
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "def-knot-exterior",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Assume countable choice, as required for the smooth normal-bundle structure in the tubular-neighbourhood interface. Let $K:S^1\\to S^3$ be a smooth oriented knot, let $\\nu(K)=TS^3|_K/TK$ be its quotient normal bundle, and let $\\Phi:\\Omega\\to S^3$ be a tubular-neighbourhood map from an open neighbourhood $\\Omega$ of the zero section in $\\nu(K)$ that restricts to the inclusion of $K$. Choose a radius $\\epsilon>0$ whose closed disk subbundle $D_\\epsilon\\nu(K)$ is contained in $\\Omega$, and set $N(K)=\\Phi(D_\\epsilon\\nu(K))$. The **exterior** of this chosen tube is $$ E_K:=S^3\\setminus\\operatorname{int}_{S^3}N(K). $$ Retain its boundary $T_K:=\\partial E_K=\\partial N(K)$, orient $E_K$ by restriction of the fixed orientation of $S^3$, and orient $T_K$ as the boundary of $E_K$. The choice of tubular map and radius is part of the input to this definition.",
