          "claim": "The endpoint permutation of $(\\sigma_1\\sigma_2^{-1})^2$ is $(12)(23)(12)(23)=(1\\ 3\\ 2)$, because each half twist has the adjacent transposition as endpoint permutation and inverse has the same transposition. By [F8], its closure is one component. Cut the standard four-crossing figure-eight diagram along its projection regions and four crossing arcs. Above and below the diagram this produces two ideal balls: each crossing arc has four face-side copies, and every face is a diagram region. Gluing upper and lower faces with the same region label restores the cut-open complement, because each cut face and crossing-arc side is identified with exactly its original mate; the only unfilled points are the deleted knot arcs, which are ideal vertices. Collapsing the two bigon faces gives two tetrahedra. Recording the vertex matches on their four faces gives exactly the four maps in the statement.",
