      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "The action preserves $|z|^2+|w|^2$, so it acts smoothly on $S^3$. The orbit of $(2^{-1/2},2^{-1/2})$ is exactly $K$. A group element stabilizes this point only if $3\\theta$ and $2\\theta$ are both multiples of $2\\pi$; coprimality of $2$ and $3$ makes the stabilizer trivial. The regions $|z|\\le|w|$ and $|w|\\le|z|$ are solid tori, parametrized respectively by $(z,w)=(z,\\sqrt{1-|z|^2}\\eta)$ and $(z,w)=(\\sqrt{1-|w|^2}\\eta,w)$ with the disk coordinate bounded by $2^{-1/2}$ and $\\eta\\in S^1$. The $w$ coordinate is the core direction of the first solid torus and winds twice along $K$; the $z$ coordinate is the core direction of the second and winds three times. This proves the claimed $(3,2)$ torus-knot type. On the axis $z=0$ the stabilizer has order $2$, and on the axis $w=0$ it has order $3$.",
