        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "On $zw\\ne0$, write $\\alpha=\\arg z$ and $\\beta=\\arg w$ modulo $2\\pi$. The integer coordinate change $\\theta=\\alpha-\\beta$, $\\phi=2\\alpha-3\\beta$ has determinant $-1$ and is invertible on the phase torus. The circle action changes $\\theta$ by its parameter and fixes $\\phi$, while $r=|z|\\in(0,1)$ is fixed; thus the quotient of this open set is the cylinder with coordinates $(r,\\phi)$, and the inverse image of any disk $D$ around $q(K)$ in it is explicitly $S^1_\\theta\\times D$. At $r=0$ and $r=1$ the phase circle collapses to one point at each end, so the full orbit space is a sphere; the two axis orbits have stabilizer orders $2$ and $3$. The complement of $D$ is a disk with those two cone points. Its orbits give the fibers of $E_K$, and [F2] identifies the axis fibers as exceptional of orders $2$ and $3$.",
